#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Unified PR/MR watcher and shared core engine for GitHub, GitLab, and Bitbucket.

Watches pull/merge requests across GitHub (github.com + GHES), GitLab (gitlab.com + self-hosted),
and Bitbucket (Cloud REST 2.0 + Server/Data Center REST 1.0) with good-citizen rate-limit
stewardship, explicit state-machine transitions, stacked PR/MR awareness, crash-safe handoff
markers, and idempotent lead remediation dispatch (`--role lead`, delegating edits to workers while running /leave-feedback and vectored review).

Usage:
  astack-watch-pr <pr-url-or-number> [watch options]
  astack-watch-pr watch <pr-url-or-number> [watch options]
  astack-watch-pr reply <pr-url-or-number> --body-file PATH --audit-receipt PATH [reply options]
  astack-watch-pr patch-id-check --before OLD_BASE..OLD_HEAD --after NEW_BASE..NEW_HEAD [--json]
  astack-watch-pr diff-guard --base REF [--head HEAD] [--baseline-lines N | --state-file PATH] [--json]
  astack-watch-pr authorship-check --before OLD_BASE..OLD_HEAD --after NEW_BASE..NEW_HEAD [--json]

Exit codes:
  0 = merge-ready, merged, --status-only/--once clean exit, --until met, or auto-dispatch complete
  1 = PR/MR closed without merging
  2 = invalid arguments, auth/not-found error, failed audit check, or another watcher holds the lock
  3 = needs rebase or branch update (merge conflicts, BEHIND, or base-branch file overlap)
  4 = needs feedback response (unresolved review threads/comments, CHANGES_REQUESTED, open tasks)
  5 = CI / pipeline check failed or cancelled
  6 = draft PR or merge gate blocked
  7 = stuck past --stuck-hours (default 24h) reminder due
  8 = timeout, rate-limit reset past --max-wait, or forge remained unreachable
"""
